# WORKCHAIN DEVELOPMENT RULES

## 1. UI & DESIGN SYSTEM RULES (Taste Skill + Impeccable)
- Use a refined dark mode aesthetic with background `#08090c` and high-contrast glassmorphism borders (`border-white/[0.08]`).
- Strict Accent Color Scheme:
  - Worker Role: Vermilion `#ff4625` / `#ff5733`
  - Client Role: Emerald `#34d399`
- DO NOT generate generic purple/pink gradients or cliché Web3 AI layouts.
- Maintain consistent Tailwind spacing (padding/margin), high contrast text ratios, and clean grid alignment.
- Always use lucide-react icons consistently.

## 2. CODE QUALITY & EFFICIENCY RULES (Anti-Slop)
- Do NOT output conversational filler, introductions, or repetitive summaries in code blocks.
- No garbage or obvious inline code comments (e.g., `// This function adds two numbers`).
- Keep TypeScript types strictly defined. Avoid using `any` when types from `viem`, `wagmi`, or `@openzeppelin/contracts` can be inferred or imported.
- Keep Solidity smart contracts clean, secure (Solidity ^0.8.20), and free from bloated docstrings.

## 3. DOCUMENTATION & COMMIT RULES (Avoid-AI-Writing)
- Write documentation and README files in a direct, professional tone without AI buzzwords (e.g., avoid "delve", "tapestry", "game-changer", "testament").
- Keep Git commit messages concise and imperative (e.g., `feat: add sbt claim button`, `fix: correct tuple unpacking in reputation contract`).